Subject: [PATCH] emacs: Match notmuch saved searches to the list's tags
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Change-Id: xzqvuqtxztrsmnmutsxrzvuululuxsvp

The saved searches query tags from an older setup: new, unread,
closed, and the patch:* review states. Nothing sets those any more.
The post-new hook derives only inbox, sent and replied from the list,
and emacs adds draft, so most of the hello screen shows empty counts
and the useful searches are buried.

Keep one search per tag that exists, plus a review queue: inbox
patches, i.e. series and replies to them that have not been answered
yet. The searches no longer pass :sort-order, which only repeated the
newest-first default that notmuch-search-oldest-first already sets.
---
Asked for in "Improve the notmuch saved searches" [1].

Dropped "flagged": synchronize_flags is off, so the tag lives only in
the local database, and the list has settled on deriving every tag
from the mail branch. The "new" entries in notmuch-search-line-faces
and notmuch-tag-formats are just as stale. They are left for a
separate patch, so this one stays to the saved searches.

Once "[PATCH v2 0/2] Archive messages that need no answer" [2] lands,
archived mail drops out of inbox, so these searches need no change.

Tested by reading init.el back in emacs --batch, and by running both
inbox queries through notmuch-saved-search-count against the list:
5 and 2. kyua tests in dotfiles/emacs fail here on unmodified trunk
too (0/25), so they say nothing about this
patch.

